# Clean Architecture — Layer Rules

This project uses **Feature-First Clean Architecture** with 3 layers per feature.

## Layer Responsibilities

| Layer | Location | Allowed |
|---|---|---|
| Domain | `features/<f>/domain/` | Entities, Repository interfaces, UseCases. Pure Dart only — no Flutter, no Dio, no framework packages. `equatable` is permitted (pure Dart utility) |
| Data | `features/<f>/data/` | Repository impls, DataSources, Models (with `fromJson`/`toEntity()`) |
| Presentation | `features/<f>/presentation/` | BLoC, Pages, Widgets. No direct API/DB calls |
| Core | `core/` | Shared infrastructure: ApiClient, DI, Router, Theme, Constants, base classes |

## The Dependency Rule

```
Presentation → Domain ← Data
```

- Domain has **zero** imports from `package:flutter`, `package:dio`, or any data/presentation file
- `package:equatable` is the **only** allowed third-party import in Domain — it is a pure Dart value-equality utility with no platform or framework dependencies
- Data depends on Domain (implements its interfaces)
- Presentation depends on Domain (calls its UseCases)
- Presentation **never** imports from `data/`
- Data **never** imports from `presentation/`

## Entities — Must Extend Equatable

All domain entities **must** extend `Equatable` and override `props`. This is required
because entities are stored inside BLoC state `props` — if entities don't implement
value equality, Equatable on the state is ineffective and BLoC will over-rebuild.

```dart
// ✅ CORRECT — entity with Equatable
class User extends Equatable {
  final String id;
  final String name;
  final String email;

  const User({required this.id, required this.name, required this.email});

  @override
  List<Object?> get props => [id, name, email];
}

// ❌ WRONG — no equality; BLoC cannot deduplicate states containing this entity
class User {
  final String id;
  final String name;
  final String email;
}
```

## Models — Do NOT Use Equatable

Models (`data/models/`) are short-lived data transfer objects. They exist only inside
the data layer, are parsed from JSON, converted via `toEntity()`, and discarded.
They are never compared, never stored in state, and never need equality logic.

```dart
// ✅ CORRECT — model without Equatable
class UserModel {
  final String id;
  final String name;
  final String email;

  factory UserModel.fromJson(Map<String, dynamic> json) => UserModel(...);
  User toEntity() => User(id: id, name: name, email: email);
}

// ❌ UNNECESSARY — don't add Equatable to models
class UserModel extends Equatable { ... }
```

## ❌ Violations

```dart
// ❌ Domain importing a framework/infrastructure package
import 'package:dio/dio.dart'; // NEVER in domain/

// ❌ BLoC importing a model
import '../../data/models/user_model.dart'; // NEVER in presentation/

// ❌ DataSource importing BLoC
import '../../presentation/bloc/auth_bloc.dart'; // NEVER in data/

// ❌ Entity without Equatable stored in BLoC state props
class Product { final String id; } // props => [product] comparison will always fail
```

## ✅ Correct Flow

```
UI (Page) → BLoC → UseCase → Repository (interface) → RepositoryImpl → DataSource → ApiClient
```

Each UseCase has one responsibility. One class, one `call()` method, one job.
